            Framework\\n\\nA WSGI-compatible micro web framework built in Python
            3.11 that provides essential web development features including URL 
            routing, request/response handling, template rendering, application 
            context management, and modular blueprints.\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n1.
            **URL Routing with Variable Segments and HTTP Method Filtering**\\n 
            - Support for dynamic URL segments like `/user/<int:id>`\\n   - HTTP
            method filtering (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.)\\n   - Flexible     
            route patterns with type converters\\n\\n2. **Request Object**\\n   
            - Encapsulates HTTP method, path, headers, query string, and body\\n
            - Easy access to request data and parameters\\n   - JSON parsing    
            support\\n\\n3. **Response Object**\\n   - Configurable status      
            codes, headers, and body content\\n   - WSGI-compatible response    
            formatting\\n   - Support for different content types\\n\\n4.       
            **Jinja2 Template Rendering**\\n   - Integrated template engine with
            application context\\n   - Automatic template loading from templates
            directory\\n   - Fallback to simple string replacement if Jinja2    
            unavailable\\n\\n5. **Application Context Management**\\n   -       
            Thread-local storage for `current_app` and `g` objects\\n   - Safe  
            concurrent request handling\\n   - Context-aware template           
            rendering\\n\\n6. **Blueprint-based Modular Applications**\\n   -   
            Organize routes into reusable blueprints\\n   - URL prefix          
            inheritance and customization\\n   - Modular application            
            architecture\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\n```bash\\npip install -e     
            .\\n```\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Basic                          
            Application\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,      
            render_template\\n\\napp =                                          
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/\')\\ndef hello():\\n    return  
            \'Hello, World!\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/user/<name>\')\\ndef           
            user_profile(name):\\n    return f\'Hello,                          
            {name}!\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/user/<int:user_id>\')\\ndef            
            user_by_id(user_id):\\n    return f\'User ID: {user_id}\'\\n\\nif   
            __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n    app.run(debug=True)\\n```\\n\\n###  
            Using Templates\\n\\nCreate a `templates/index.html`                
            file:\\n```html\\n<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html>\\n<head>\\n    <title>{{ 
            title }}</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n    <h1>{{ heading }}</h1>\\n 
            <p>Welcome, {{ name                                                 
            }}!</p>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n```\\n\\n```python\\nfrom             
            flaskframework import Flask, render_template\\n\\napp =             
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/welcome/<name>\')\\ndef          
            welcome(name):\\n    return render_template(\'index.html\', \\n     
            title=\'Welcome Page\',\\n                                          
            heading=\'Welcome!\',\\n                         name=name)\\n\\nif 
            __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n    app.run()\\n```\\n\\n### Using      
            Blueprints\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,       
            Blueprint\\n\\n# Create a blueprint\\napi = Blueprint(\'api\',      
            __name__, url_prefix=\'/api\')\\n\\n@api.route(\'/users\')\\ndef    
            list_users():\\n    return \'List of                                
            users\'\\n\\n@api.route(\'/users/<int:user_id>\')\\ndef             
            get_user(user_id):\\n    return f\'User {user_id}\'\\n\\n# Create   
            main app and register blueprint\\napp =                             
            Flask(__name__)\\napp.register_blueprint(api)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/\')
            \\ndef index():\\n    return \'Main page\'\\n\\nif __name__ ==      
